# Command pyside6

## What does this command do:

Qt6 Python bindings — build cross-platform desktop GUIs with Python using the full Qt framework. Includes a suite of CLI tools for compiling UI files, resources, translations, and deploying applications.

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: `pip install --user pyside6`

To upgrade: `pip install --user --upgrade pyside6`

## Command path

For Fedora run: ~/.local/bin/pyside6-*  (family of tools, all at this location)

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/

## Command options

# --- pyside6-designer ---
# Visual GUI editor — drag and drop widgets, save as .ui files
pyside6-designer
pyside6-designer mywindow.ui

# --- pyside6-uic (UI compiler) ---
# Convert .ui file (from Designer) to Python class
pyside6-uic mainwindow.ui -o ui_mainwindow.py

# Generate to stdout
pyside6-uic mainwindow.ui

# --- pyside6-rcc (Resource compiler) ---
# Compile a .qrc resource file into a Python module
pyside6-rcc resources.qrc -o rc_resources.py

# Output to stdout
pyside6-rcc resources.qrc

# --- pyside6-qml ---
# Run a QML file directly
pyside6-qml main.qml

# --- pyside6-lrelease (Translation release) ---
# Compile .ts translation source to binary .qm
pyside6-lrelease translations/app_de.ts -qm app_de.qm

# --- pyside6-lupdate (Translation update) ---
# Extract translatable strings from Python/QML sources into .ts files
pyside6-lupdate main.py -ts translations/app_de.ts

# --- pyside6-deploy ---
# Package a PySide6 app into a standalone executable
pyside6-deploy main.py

# Deploy with a specific config file
pyside6-deploy main.py -c pysidedeploy.spec

# Android deploy
pyside6-android-deploy --name MyApp --mode release

# --- pyside6-genpyi ---
# Generate .pyi stub files for IDE autocompletion
pyside6-genpyi all

# --- pyside6-project ---
# Manage a PySide6 project (build, clean, run)
pyside6-project build
pyside6-project run
pyside6-project clean

